WEBVTT

1
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.160
Well struck.

2
00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.860
Well struck. dog.

3
00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.730
Did you like that?

4
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.710
It was well struck. Your Grace.

5
00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.210
I already said it was well struck.

6
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.180
Yes. Your Grace.

7
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.220
- Who's next?

8
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.220
- Lothor Brune.

9
00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.490
freerider in the service of Lord Baelish.

10
00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.720
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard.

11
00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.460
Ser Dontos the Red of House Hollard!

12
00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.970
Here I am.

13
00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.030
Here I am.

14
00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.870
Sorry. Your Grace.

15
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.710
My deepest apologies.

16
00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.380
- Are you drunk?

17
00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.380
- No.

18
00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:11.180
No. No. Your Grace.

19
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.880
- I had two cups of wine.

20
00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.880
- Two cups?

21
00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.860
That's not much at all.

22
00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:18.590
Please. have another cup.

23
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.130
Are you sure. Your Grace?

24
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.490
Yes. To celebrate my name day.

25
00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.000
Have two. Have as much as you like.

26
00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:27.890
I would be honored. Your Grace.

27
00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:32.600
Ser Meryn. help Ser Dontos

28
00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:32.600
celebrate my name day.

29
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.740
See that he drinks his fill.

30
00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.890
You can't.

31
00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.090
What did you say?

32
00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:00.270
Did you say I can't?

33
00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.890
I only meant

34
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.870
it would be bad luck

35
00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.870
to kill a man on your name day.

36
00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.100
What kind of stupid peasant's superstition...

37
00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.040
The girl is right.

38
00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.450
What a man sows on his name day.

39
00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:12.450
he reaps all year.

40
00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.380
Take him away.

41
00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:19.510
I'll have him killed tomorrow. the fool.

42
00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.120
He is a fool.

43
00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:26.120
You're so clever to see it.

44
00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.390
He'll make a much better fool than a knight.

45
00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.460
He doesn't deserve

46
00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.460
the mercy of a quick death.

47
00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.000
Did you hear my lady. Ser Dontos?

48
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.130
From this day. you'll be my new fool.

49
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.400
Thank you. Your Grace.

50
00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:45.640
And you. my lady. thank you.

51
00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.340
Beloved nephew.

52
00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.420
We looked for you on the battlefield.

53
00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.050
You were nowhere to be found.

54
00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:05.660
I've been here. ruling the kingdoms.

55
00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.360
What a fine job you've done.

56
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.530
Look at you.

57
00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.200
More beautiful than ever.

58
00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.010
And you!

59
00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.340
You're going to be bigger than the Hound.

60
00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.810
but much better looking.

61
00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.820
This one doesn't like me.

62
00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.750
Can't imagine why.

63
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.310
- We heard you were dead.

64
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.310
- I'm glad you're not dead.

65
00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.990
Me. too. dear. Death is so boring.

66
00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.360
especially now.

67
00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.360
with so much excitement in the world.

68
00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.700
My lady. I'm sorry for your loss.

69
00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.870
Her loss?

70
00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.870
Her father was a confessed traitor.

71
00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.530
But still her father.

72
00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.230
Surely. having so recently lost your own

73
00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.230
beloved father. you can sympathize.

74
00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.450
My father was a traitor.

75
00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.380
My mother and brother are traitors. too.

76
00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:57.980
I am loyal to my beloved Joffrey.

77
00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.950
Of course you are.

78
00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.830
Well. enjoy your name day. Your Grace.

79
00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:09.590
Wish I could stay and celebrate.

80
00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:12.460
but there is work to be done.

81
00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:14.530
What work?

82
00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.570
Why are you here?

83
00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.840
A raven arrived from the citadel

84
00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.840
this morning. Your Grace.

85
00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:27.610
The conclave has met.

86
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.120
considered reports from maesters

87
00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:31.120
all over the Seven Kingdoms.

88
00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.350
and declared this great summer

89
00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.280
done at last.

90
00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:40.120
The longest summer in living memory.

91
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.790
The peasants say. a long summer means

92
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.790
an even longer winter.

93
00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:45.630
A common superstition.

94
00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:48.100
We have enough wheat for a five-year winter.

95
00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.500
If it lasts any longer.

96
00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.040
we'll have fewer peasants.

97
00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.510
The city's drowning in refugees.

98
00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.510
Your Grace. fleeing the war.

99
00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.640
We have nowhere to house them.

100
00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.640
And with winter coming. it'll only get worse.

101
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:03.010
You command the city watch.

102
00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:03.010
do you not. Lord Slynt?

103
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:06.120
I do. Your Grace.

104
00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.180
And are you not a lord at my command?

105
00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:11.850
I owe my title and lands

106
00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:11.850
to your generosity. Your Grace.

107
00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.450
Then do your job.

108
00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.450
Shut the gates to the peasants.

109
00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.430
They belong in the field. not our capital.

110
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.090
Yes. Your Grace.

111
00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.900
Don't get up.

112
00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.940
More ravishing than ever. big sister.

113
00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.920
War agrees with you.

114
00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:38.510
Forgive the interruption. Carry on.

115
00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:41.480
What are you doing here?

116
00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.220
It's been a remarkable journey.

117
00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.850
I pissed off the edge of the Wall.

118
00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.800
I slept in a sky cell.

119
00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.060
I fought with the hill tribes.

120
00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.660
So many adventures.

121
00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.530
so much to be thankful for.

122
00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.510
What are you doing here?

123
00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:03.510
This is the small council.

124
00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.310
Yes. well. I do believe the Hand of the King

125
00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:08.310
is welcome at all small council meetings.

126
00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.110
Our father is Hand of the King.

127
00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:13.180
Yes. but in his absence...

128
00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.900
Your father has named Lord Tyrion

129
00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.490
to serve as hand in his stead while he fights.

130
00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:28.000
Out! All of you out!

131
00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.570
I would like to know

132
00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.570
how you tricked Father into this.

133
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:39.170
If I were capable of tricking Father.

134
00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:39.170
I'd be emperor of the world by now.

135
00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.820
You brought this on yourself.

136
00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.310
I've done nothing.

137
00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.220
Quite right. you did nothing

138
00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.520
when your son called for Ned Stark's head.

139
00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:49.560
Now the entire North has risen up against us.

140
00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:52.060
- I tried to stop it.

141
00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:52.060
- Did you? You failed.

142
00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.330
That bit of theater

143
00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.330
will haunt our family for a generation.

144
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.270
- Robb Stark is a child.

145
00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:59.270
- Who's won every battle he's fought.

146
00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.730
Do you understand we're losing the war?

147
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.860
- What do you know about warfare?

148
00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.860
- Nothing.

149
00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.700
But I know people.

150
00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.440
And I know that our enemies hate each other

151
00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:11.440
almost as much as they hate us.

152
00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.710
- Joffrey is king.

153
00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:21.150
You are here to advise him.

154
00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:22.880
I'm only here to advise him.

155
00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.490
And if the king listens to what I say.

156
00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.050
the king might just get his Uncle Jaime back.

157
00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:32.330
How?

158
00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.960
You love your children.

159
00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.060
It's your one redeeming quality.

160
00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:37.060
That and your cheekbones.

161
00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:41.410
The Starks love their children as well.

162
00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.710
- And we have two of them.

163
00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.710
- One.

164
00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:48.410
- One?

165
00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:48.410
- Arya. little animal. she disappeared.

166
00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.480
Disappeared? What. in a puff of smoke?

167
00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:56.560
We had three Starks to trade.

168
00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.250
You chopped one's head off

169
00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.250
and let another escape.

170
00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:02.320
Father will be furious.

171
00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.970
It must be odd for you

172
00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:09.940
to be the disappointing child.

173
00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:21.240
My lord. may the old gods

174
00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:21.240
watch over your brother

175
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.980
and all our Northern sons.

176
00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:27.890
The walls of my holdfast

177
00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:27.890
will not stand the winter.

178
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.090
The stones were last mortared

179
00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:32.090
in the time of King Aerys.

180
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.760
and I'm afraid the masons today

181
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.760
are not fit to carry their fathers' hammers.

182
00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:39.590
When I was a boy.

183
00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:45.070
I remember seeing them put up a new tower

184
00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:45.070
at Torrhen's Square in a summer.

185
00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:47.110
Men worked back then.

186
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:52.480
Today. my holdfast looks like it was built

187
00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:52.480
by drunk children.

188
00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:56.640
At night you can hear the wind

189
00:10:52.550 --> 00:10:56.640
howling through the gaps.

190
00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:59.010
Gods forbid it rains.

191
00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.920
Why. I might as well sleep beneath a waterfall.

192
00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:06.890
Maintenance of a holdfast generally falls

193
00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:06.890
to the lord of that holdfast.

194
00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.500
Generally. yes.

195
00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.020
but I've sent all the young men off

196
00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.020
to fight Robb Stark's war.

197
00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:15.230
King Robb. And it's not his war.

198
00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.170
He didn't choose it.

199
00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.770
Maybe not. my lord.

200
00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.770
but he called in his banners and took the men.

201
00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.500
Joffrey killed my father.

202
00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.010
your liege lord.

203
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.480
Do you remember your vows. ser?

204
00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:29.420
Of course I remember!

205
00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.510
We can spare four masons

206
00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.510
for a week. my lord.

207
00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:35.580
Will that be sufficient to repair your walls?

208
00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.680
I believe it will.

209
00:11:43.900 --> 00:11:46.630
We didn't want him here all day. did we?

210
00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.510
I didn't like the way

211
00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.510
he was talking about Robb.

212
00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.230
Nor did I.

213
00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.610
But listening to people

214
00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.610
you'd rather not listen to

215
00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.580
is one of your responsibilities

216
00:11:57.680 --> 00:12:01.580
as Lord of Winterfell.

217
00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.920
Lord Portan.

218
00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.890
My lord. may the old gods

219
00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.890
watch over your brother

220
00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:11.650
and all our Northern sons.

221
00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:04.040
Boil this for an hour and drink the tea.

222
00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:07.550
Makes all your pain go away.

223
00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:09.110
Don't have any pain.

224
00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:11.720
Lucky for you.

225
00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.290
That way.

226
00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:19.820
You've been having those dreams again.

227
00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:21.560
I don't dream.

228
00:13:21.630 --> 00:13:23.150
Everyone dreams.

229
00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.790
I don't.

230
00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.190
Heard some of the men

231
00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.190
talking about the comet.

232
00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.530
They say it's an omen.

233
00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:34.040
They say it means Robb

234
00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:34.040
will win a great victory in the South.

235
00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.540
Did they?

236
00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:41.170
I heard some other fools say

237
00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:41.170
it's Lannister Red.

238
00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.410
Means the Lannisters

239
00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:44.410
will rule all Seven Kingdoms before long.

240
00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.940
Heard a stable boy say it's the color of blood

241
00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:50.180
to mark the death of your father.

242
00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:57.360
The stars don't fall for men.

243
00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:59.870
Red comet means one thing. boy.

244
00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:02.570
Dragons.

245
00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:07.370
The dragons are all dead.

246
00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.780
They've been dead for centuries.

247
00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:55.750
What did your brother say

248
00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:55.750
about them. Khaleesi?

249
00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.490
He said they ate meat.

250
00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:00.150
He didn't tell you what kind of meat?

251
00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.230
My brother didn't know

252
00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.230
anything about dragons.

253
00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.290
He didn't know anything about anything.

254
00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:43.240
She was Drogo's first gift to me.

255
00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.000
I remember.

256
00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.770
I promised to protect them.

257
00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.110
Promised them

258
00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:53.110
their enemies would die screaming.

259
00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.580
How do I make starvation scream?

260
00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:58.380
A trick I never learned. I'm afraid.

261
00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.720
Does it ever end?

262
00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.660
This is further east than I've ever been.

263
00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.790
But. yes. Khaleesi.

264
00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.790
everything ends. even the Red Waste.

265
00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.330
And you're sure there's no other way?

266
00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.030
If we go south to the land of the Lhazareen.

267
00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.590
the Lamb Men will kill us

268
00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.590
and take your dragons.

269
00:16:15.670 --> 00:16:17.470
If we go west to the Dothraki Sea.

270
00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:21.170
the first khalasar we meet

271
00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:21.170
will kill us and take your dragons.

272
00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.640
No one will take my dragons.

273
00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:27.680
They are too weak to fight.

274
00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.810
as are your people.

275
00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.980
You must be their strength.

276
00:16:33.090 --> 00:16:35.020
As you are mine.

277
00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.670
Rakharo. Aggo. Kovarro.

278
00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.670
Take our remaining horses.

279
00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:56.180
You will ride east. you southeast.

280
00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:56.180
and you northeast.

281
00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.540
What do we seek. Khaleesi?

282
00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:05.750
Cities. living or dead. Caravans and people.

283
00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:05.750
Rivers or lakes or the great salt sea.

284
00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:11.420
Find how far the Red Waste extends

285
00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:11.420
before us. and what lies on the other side.

286
00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.730
Rakharo.

287
00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:27.810
You are my last hope. blood of my blood.

288
00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.380
I will not fail you. blood of my blood.

289
00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.310
You never have.

290
00:17:39.650 --> 00:17:42.750
This is bad time to start.

291
00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:41.120
Having a rough time of it?

292
00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.710
Nothing's killed me yet.

293
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.450
- Your arse killed the sledge.

294
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:45.450
- You offered me a ride.

295
00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.460
I just wanted you to shut up

296
00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.460
